          "text": "<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# claudeMd\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of D:\\workspace\\gitlab\\hbec-acnt-zsyyt-git\\CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# CLAUDE.md\r\n\r\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\r\n\r\n## Repository Overview\r\n\r\nThis is a Java-based web application built with Spring Framework 4.2, designed as a掌上营业厅 (Mobile Business Hall) system. The application follows a business process-oriented architecture where each business function is defined as a configurable process with multiple steps.\r\n\r\n## Key Technologies & Frameworks\r\n\r\n- Java 8\r\n- Spring Framework 4.2 (MVC, Core, JDBC, Transaction Management)\r\n- Maven for build management\r\n- JSP for views\r\n- MySQL for database\r\n- Redis for session management\r\n- Custom business process engine (ApexSoft extended process framework)\r\n\r\n## Architecture Overview\r\n\r\n### Core Components\r\n\r\n1. **Business Process Engine**: Custom XML-based process configuration system that defines business workflows with steps, handlers, and callbacks.\r\n\r\n2. **Handler System**: Risk validation components that check various conditions before allowing business processes to proceed (e.g., customer status, ongoing applications, document types).\r\n\r\n3. **Step-Based UI Flow**: Multi-step user interface flows where each step corresponds to a phase in the business process.\r\n\r\n4. **Data Objects**: Business-specific data transfer objects defined in XML configurations and corresponding Java classes.\r\n\r\n### Directory Structure\r\n\r\n- `src/main/java`: Java source code organized by packages\r\n- `src/main/resources`: Configuration files including business process definitions\r\n- `src/main/webapp`: Web resources (JSPs, CSS, JS, images)\r\n- `src/test`: Unit and integration tests\r\n\r\n### Business Process Configuration\r\n\r\nBusiness processes are defined in XML files located at `src/main/resources/huabao/business/`. Each file represents one business function (e.g., password reset, account activation) with:\r\n- Process metadata (ID, name, codes)\r\n- Data type definitions\r\n- Risk validation handlers\r\n- Step definitions with navigation flow\r\n- Callback references\r\n\r\nThese are imported and registered in `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`.\r\n\r\n## Common Development Commands\r\n\r\n### Building the Project\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Compile and package the WAR file\r\nmvn clean package\r\n\r\n# Package with assembly (creates tar archive)\r\nmvn clean package -DskipTests\r\n\r\n# Run with embedded Tomcat\r\nmvn tomcat7:run\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Running Tests\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Run all unit tests\r\nmvn test\r\n\r\n# Run a specific test class\r\nmvn test -Dtest=TestClassName\r\n\r\n# Skip tests during build\r\nmvn package -DskipTests\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Resource Compression\r\n\r\nThe project includes a Node.js script for compressing JavaScript and CSS files:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Install dependencies\r\nnpm install\r\n\r\n# Run compression script between two commits/branches\r\nnode minify-diff.js [branch] [tag]\r\nnode minify-diff.js [commitId] [commitIid]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Working with Business Processes\r\n\r\nBusiness processes are configured in XML files. To add a new business process:\r\n1. Create a new XML file in `src/main/resources/huabao/business/`\r\n2. Define the process with steps, handlers, and callbacks\r\n3. Import the file in `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`\r\n4. Implement corresponding Java callback classes if needed\r\n\r\n## Configuration Files\r\n\r\n- `pom.xml`: Maven build configuration\r\n- `src/main/resources/springMVC.xml`: Main Spring configuration\r\n- `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`: Business process imports\r\n- `src/main/resources/package-resource.xml`: Assembly packaging configuration\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n"
