usiness process definitions\r\n- `src/main/webapp`: Web resources (JSPs, CSS, JS, images)\r\n- `src/test`: Unit and integration tests\r\n\r\n### Business Process Configuration\r\n\r\nBusiness processes are defined in XML files located at `src/main/resources/huabao/business/`. Each file represents one business function (e.g., password reset, account activation) with:\r\n- Process metadata (ID, name, codes)\r\n- Data type definitions\r\n- Risk validation handlers\r\n- Step definitions with navigation flow\r\n- Callback references\r\n\r\nThese are imported and registered in `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`.\r\n\r\n## Common Development Commands\r\n\r\n### Building the Project\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Compile and package the WAR file\r\nmvn clean package\r\n\r\n# Package with assembly (creates tar archive)\r\nmvn clean package -DskipTests\r\n\r\n# Run with embedded Tomcat\r\nmvn tomcat7:run\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Running Tests\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Run all unit tests\r\nmvn test\r\n\r\n# Run a specific test class\r\nmvn test -Dtest=TestClassName\r\n\r\n# Skip tests during build\r\nmvn package -DskipTests\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Resource Compression\r\n\r\nThe project includes a Node.js script for compressing JavaScript and CSS files:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Install dependencies\r\nnpm install\r\n\r\n# Run compression script between two commits/branches\r\nnode minify-diff.js [branch] [tag]\r\nnode minify-diff.js [commitId] [commitIid]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Working with Business Processes\r\n\r\nBusiness processes are configured in XML files. To add a new business process:\r\n1. Create a new XML file in `src/main/resources/huabao/business/`\r\n2. Define the process with steps, handlers, and callbacks\r\n3. Import the file in `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`\r\n4. Implement corresponding Java callback classes if needed\r\n\r\n## Configuration Files\r\n\r\n- `pom.xml`: Maven build configuration\r\n- `src/main/resources/springMVC.xml`: Main Spring configuration\r\n- `src/main/resources/huabao/businessConfig.xml`: Business process imports\r\n- `src/main/resources/package-resource.xml`: Assembly packaging configuration\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n"
